      <h2 data-dc-tpl="176" style="color: rgb(246, 239, 228); font-family: &quot;Archivo Black&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: clamp(28px, 5.5vw, 46px); line-height: 1.02; margin: 8px 0px 0px; text-transform: uppercase;">Mexican family...Mexican kitchen.</h2>
      <p data-dc-tpl="177" style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(234, 226, 214, 0.78); margin: 14px 0px 0px; max-width: 52ch;">There is nothing more authentically Mexican than this. Homemade corn and flour tortillas, homemade salsas, and fresh, hot, chopped meats daily. This is the only truly authentic Mexican restaurant in Montgomery County.</p>
      <p data-dc-tpl="178" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(234, 226, 214, 0.85); margin: 12px 0px 18px; max-width: 52ch;">Two brothers from Mexico, cooking the food they grew up with. Not a chain, not a franchise, and no relation to the Señor Tequila’s in Virginia (please don’t get confused). The Rivas brothers have owned the brand since 2002 and still run the room.</p>
